adr: 0208
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: break_continue
why: AP 6.7.5.10 NOTE 1 terminates the closest-containing repetitive-statement and no other. Not restoring the enclosing loop's targets after a body leaves the inner loop's blocks in scope for the outer one, so a later break in the outer loop branches into blocks that are no longer reachable -- and the nested case's count is wrong rather than the module being invalid, which is what makes this worth a file.
--- old
  breakBlock := savedBrk;
  contBlock := savedCnt;
  writeln(ircode, '  br label %L', contB:1);
  StartBlock(contB);
--- new
  writeln(ircode, '  br label %L', contB:1);
  StartBlock(contB);
